Package: copykat
Type: Package
Title: COPYKAT: Inference of genomic copy number and subclonal
        structure of human tumors from high-throughput single cell
        RNA-seq data (rat rn7 fork)
Version: 1.1.0.9001
Author: Ruli Gao
Maintainer: Ruli Gao <ruli.gao@northwestern.edu>
Description: COPYKAT is a computational tool using integrative Bayesian approaches to identify genome-wide aneuploidy at 5MB resolution in single cells to separate aneuploid (tumor) cells from diploid (normal) cells, and tumor subclones using high-throughput sc-RNAseq data. This fork adds a rat (Rattus norvegicus, mRatBN7.2) gene-space code path via genome="rn7", reusing the mouse (mm10) downstream branch with a rat annotation table (full.anno.rn7). Based on copykat 1.1.0, upstream commit b795ff793522499f814f6ae282aad1aab790902f.
License: GPL-2
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: false
Imports: parallel, parallelDist, dlm, gplots, RColorBrewer, mixtools,
        cluster, MCMCpack
RoxygenNote: 7.1.2
NeedsCompilation: no
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
